{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Therefore</b> — <b>my heart</b> is the intellect of knowledge." "<b>And my glory</b> — the soul." "<b>Also my flesh</b> — the body. The explanation: for since he cleaves to the supernal power, his soul exults, and the power of cleaving to Him guards him from illnesses in the change of the future; therefore his body dwells in this world in security."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:21.648763912Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}